    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on exploiting favorable pitching matchups to maximize offensive output. Our top play is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.39), who benefits from a prime matchup against Fisher and a significant dynamic platoon advantage, making him a high-efficiency anchor for the middle infield. **Drake Baldwin** (69.55) and **Jacob Wilson** (63.95) also grade out as elite starts; **Drake Baldwin** faces a vulnerable Ed Rodriguez, while **Jacob Wilson** leverages a 10% park factor boost against the lefty MacKenzie Gore. **Heliot Ramos** (62.74) rounds out the top tier, as his ability to capitalize on Fisher\u2019s slow delivery significantly increases his stolen base ceiling\u2014a critical factor for our team strategy.\n\nThe most difficult decision of the day involved **Gunnar Henderson**, who was narrowly benched with a score of 43.19. Despite his talent, he faces a tough matchup against I. Seymour, and the optimizer penalized his projected efficiency due to the southpaw hurdle and a less-than-ideal park factor. Meanwhile, we are monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses closely: **Wade Meckler** (59.97) and **Sam Antonacci** (58.49) are both poised for strong days batting atop the order against Melton, assuming they lead off as projected. We have mitigated risk by benching **Andy Pages** (49.92) in favor of higher-efficiency hitters, as his matchup against the elite 2.03 xERA of Jacob Misiorowski makes him a secondary option despite his power profile. We remain thin at the corners with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** sidelined on the IL, but with **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Kyle Tucker** also unavailable, the current roster must aggressively pursue these stolen base opportunities against catchers with longer pop times to keep the Roto lead intact.",
